  {:block/id #uuid "6a5ad3b1-2038-4402-9e92-2ee7d24375d7",
   :block/page-name "Jul 9th, 2026",
   :block/properties nil,
   :block/children
   ({:block/id #uuid "6a5ad3b1-e2a6-4807-a6c5-046aaef39730",
     :block/properties nil,
     :block/format :markdown,
     :block/children [],
     :block/content "First logseq journal"}
    {:block/id #uuid "6a5ad3b1-d735-4aa5-b4af-e5aaffaa2b08",
     :block/properties nil,
     :block/format :markdown,
     :block/children [],
     :block/content ""}
    {:block/id #uuid "6a5ad3b1-6ca5-4114-8849-2d5335a38dc6",
     :block/properties nil,
     :block/format :markdown,
     :block/children [],
     :block/content
     "Is it possible to create a website that required authorization to connect, and further authentication to connect. After verification has been passed, the website will provide Filezila UI like, that enable ssh file share from the termux server?"}
    {:block/id #uuid "6a5ad3b1-ab1d-477e-acd6-c12e26665a0f",
     :block/properties nil,
     :block/format :markdown,
     :block/children [],
     :block/content ""}
    {:block/id #uuid "6a5ad3b1-c1d5-4e77-abf3-79c929487b15",
     :block/properties nil,
     :block/format :markdown,
     :block/children [],
     :block/content ""}
    {:block/id #uuid "6a5ad3b1-4c5b-4245-acb9-2b123df38692",
     :block/properties nil,
     :block/format :markdown,
     :block/children [],
     :block/content ""}
    {:block/id #uuid "6a5ad3b1-3e37-4a0b-8eb0-ff3c7e00838b",
     :block/properties nil,
     :block/format :markdown,
     :block/children [],
     :block/content
     "Yes, it is absolutely possible to build a website with this exact functionality. You're describing a secure, web-based SFTP client that acts as a gateway to a Termux server."}
    {:block/id #uuid "6a5ad3b1-9504-4e91-bd89-389778f0bf32",
     :block/properties nil,
     :block/format :markdown,
     :block/children [],
     :block/content
     "Here’s a breakdown of how this can be achieved, from the authorization layer to the FileZilla-like interface."}
    {:block/id #uuid "6a5ad3b1-d679-487b-add3-eb6421151c93",
     :block/properties nil,
     :block/format :markdown,
     :block/children [],
     :block/content
     "🛡️ Step 1: Authorization & Authentication (The Security Layer)"}
    {:block/id #uuid "6a5ad3b1-3092-4b1c-9d03-0981b5da9275",
     :block/properties nil,
     :block/format :markdown,
     :block/children [],
     :block/content
     "Your website will need two layers of security, which can be implemented in a few ways:"}
    {:block/id #uuid "6a5ad3b1-7eea-4c1f-8a7b-826915359a91",
     :block/properties nil,
     :block/format :markdown,
     :block/children [],
     :block/content
     "· Application-Level Authentication: The website itself will require users to log in. This can be as simple as a basic username and password (HTTP Basic Auth) or a more robust system with user management. Many web-based file managers have this built-in.\n· Server-Level Authentication (SSH): After logging into the website, the application will use the provided credentials to establish a secure SSH connection to your Termux server. This is typically done using the SFTP (SSH File Transfer Protocol).\n· Alternative: One-Time Tokens: For enhanced security, you could generate time-sensitive tokens for each session, providing an extra layer of verification."}
    {:block/id #uuid "6a5ad3b1-73d9-4771-8a17-aae9132f3b4b",
     :block/properties nil,
     :block/format :markdown,
     :block/children [],
     :block/content
     "💻 Step 2: The FileZilla-like Interface (The User Experience)"}
    {:block/id #uuid "6a5ad3b1-3815-4c0f-aa7a-1e261fde5f66",
     :block/properties nil,
     :block/format :markdown,
     :block/children [],
     :block/content
     "To create a dual-pane file manager experience in a web browser, you can use several ready-made solutions:"}
    {:block/id #uuid "6a5ad3b1-42dd-49d2-ad77-8f173e258b90",
     :block/properties nil,
     :block/format :markdown,
     :block/children [],
     :block/content
     "· FileZilla in a Container (Docker): You can run a Docker container that hosts a full FileZilla client accessible via a web browser. This can be set up with its own web GUI authentication.\n· Cloud Commander: An open-source, dual-panel web file manager that runs on Node.js. It includes optional authorization, works on Android via Termux, and can manage files.\n· Other Web-Based File Managers: Several open-source projects are designed for this purpose:\n· Filebrowser: A web-based file manager that can be configured with basic authentication.\n· Filex-Termux: A lightweight web-based file explorer specifically for Termux.\n· GAGU: A web-based file management system that works on Android/Termux."}
    {:block/id #uuid "6a5ad3b1-ee6a-4fac-97e1-01562f26bd3a",
     :block/properties nil,
     :block/format :markdown,
     :block/children [],
     :block/content
     "🔌 Step 3: Connecting to the Termux Server (The Backend)"}
    {:block/id #uuid "6a5ad3b1-b5fc-4152-af98-dbc985380cb0",
     :block/properties nil,
     :block/format :markdown,
     :block/children [],
     :block/content
     "For your website to connect to the Termux server via SSH/SFTP, the backend (e.g., a Node.js server) will need to use an SSH/SFTP library. It will use the credentials from Step 1 to establish a secure connection and perform file operations."}
    {:block/id #uuid "6a5ad3b1-56e0-4bd5-bec7-81bfd131bcd5",
     :block/properties nil,
     :block/format :markdown,
     :block/children [],
     :block/content "📝 Summary & Recommendation"}
    {:block/id #uuid "6a5ad3b1-38f7-44e2-8dea-7921d50181c2",
     :block/properties nil,
     :block/format :markdown,
     :block/children [],
     :block/content
     "A practical way to achieve this is by using Cloud Commander:"}
    {:block/id #uuid "6a5ad3b1-42de-4ae4-8054-ec31c861962d",
     :block/properties nil,
     :block/format :markdown,
     :block/children [],
     :block/content
     "1. Install Termux on your Android device and set up an SSH server.\n2. Install Node.js and Cloud Commander on your Termux environment.\n3. Enable authorization in Cloud Commander to create your first security layer.\n4. Configure Cloud Commander to connect to your Termux server's SSH/SFTP service, which acts as the second authentication layer."}
    {:block/id #uuid "6a5ad3b1-fd19-4427-8a5b-2b952ce7710e",
     :block/properties nil,
     :block/format :markdown,
     :block/children [],
     :block/content
     "This approach gives you a web-based, dual-pane file manager (Step 2) with built-in security (Step 1) that can connect to your Termux server (Step 3)."}
    {:block/id #uuid "6a5ad3b1-be80-4e71-8613-355a0fe3975e",
     :block/properties nil,
     :block/format :markdown,
     :block/children [],
     :block/content "⚠️ Important Security Considerations"}
    {:block/id #uuid "6a5ad3b1-4e43-42ae-9140-e56c495652fa",
     :block/properties nil,
     :block/format :markdown,
     :block/children [],
     :block/content
     "· Never expose a file manager without any authentication or sandboxing to the public internet.\n· Always use strong, unique passwords.\n· For the highest security, consider using SSH key-based authentication instead of passwords."})})}
